<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">tempo</ansi>

Speed, your personal burden and your armor's bulk set how often you act in
combat. Everyone
gets one opening turn. After that a slow fighter sometimes skips a round;
a fast fighter sometimes gets two turns. Formation and your target's Speed
do not set your tempo. Cargo and horses never make your worn gear lighter
(<ansi fg="command">help burden</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The action meter</ansi>

Each combat round fills your meter by 100 times your tempo. Each full 100
pays for one turn. Tempo is between {{ config "GamePlay.Combat.TempoMin" }} and {{ config "GamePlay.Combat.TempoMax" }} turns per round,
with at most {{ config "GamePlay.Combat.MaxTurnsPerRound" }} turns in any round. Afterward at most 99 points carry
forward. You cannot bank whole turns for a burst. The meter ends with the
fight and starts fresh in the next one, including after a server restart.
A Samurai opens each battle with half a turn already on its meter (Iaijutsu),
and gains half a turn when it fells a foe (Zanshin, from level 8): see
<ansi fg="command">help samurai</ansi>.

At Speed {{ config "GamePlay.Combat.TempoSpeedRef" }}, without burden, your tempo is one. Each {{ config "GamePlay.Combat.TempoSpeedSpan" }} extra Speed
adds one before the cap. Full personal burden reduces this rate by 35%. Medium armor then takes
{{ configpct "GamePlay.Combat.BulkTempoMedium" }}% of it and heavy armor {{ configpct "GamePlay.Combat.BulkTempoHeavy" }}%, twice that in armor heavier than your
training (<ansi fg="command">help armor</ansi>).
An attacks bonus adds 0.1 tempo per point before burden and the cap.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What a turn contains</ansi>

One turn is your normal weapon attack: both eligible hands and each
weapon's own strikes. Unarmed attacks and claws use the same tempo rules.
A tackle spends one turn, hit or miss. An opening strike or aimed shot
replaces one attack turn; a second earned turn is an ordinary attack.

Chants advance once per combat round, regardless of tempo. While chanting
you make no weapon attack, including the round the chant ends or breaks.
Weapon waits decrement once per round. Physical wind-ups prepare and
release on separate rounds and occupy the whole round. Statuses that
cost your actions cost all earned turns for that round. Those turns are
lost; the meter retains only fractional progress.

Guards and shield counters are reactions and spend no meter. Their existing
limits still apply. Tempo never advances the world's clock.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help speed</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help burden</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help armor</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help abilities</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help interrupts</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>.

If your foe falls before your earned physical turn, you (and each companion)
turn to another reachable member of that enemy group and use the turn; enemies
do the same against your company. A kill can also leave a second earned turn
for the next foe.
